        "t": "chr",
        "v": [
          "This module classifies repository files and, for tabular data files available locally, extracts each column's type and summary statistics.",
          "#### Data Tree",
          "Where the files sit within each repository. Each file is followed by how it was classified, which study it belongs to.",
          "**Repository: https://osf.io/schem**",
          "```\n├── pp1.csv      📊 data ex1\n├── pp2.csv      📊 data ex1\n├── pp3.csv      📊 data ex1\n└── summary.csv  📊 data ex1\n```",
          "#### Data Files",
          "::: {.panel-tabset}\n\n## pp1.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(trial = 1:6, q3 = c(513L, 499L, 611L, 578L, 531L, \n490L), v7 = c(1L, 2L, 3L, 1L, 2L, 3L)), row.names = c(NA, 6L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n## pp2.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(trial = 1:6, q3 = c(514L, 500L, 612L, 579L, 532L, \n491L), v7 = c(1L, 2L, 3L, 1L, 2L, 3L)), row.names = c(NA, 6L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n## pp3.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(trial = 1:6, q3 = c(515L, 501L, 613L, 580L, 533L, \n492L), v7 = c(1L, 2L, 3L, 1L, 2L, 3L)), row.names = c(NA, 6L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n## summary.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(pid = 1:3, q3 = c(20L, 30L, 40L), note = c(\"a\", \n\"b\", \"c\")), row.names = c(NA, 3L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n:::",
          "#### Descriptives Overview\n\nWe found 0 columns with at least one missing value.",
          "::: {.panel-tabset}\n\n## summary.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Column = c(\"note\", \"pid\", \"q3\"), Representation = c(\"text\", \n\"text\", \"numeric\"), Level = c(\"nominal\", \"nominal\", \"ratio\"), \n    Concept = c(\"\", \"id\", \"reaction_time\"), Role = c(\"measure\", \n    \"identifier\", \"measure\"), Unit = c(\"\", \"\", \"\"), Rows = c(3L, \n    3L, 3L), \"% Missing\" = c(0, 0, 0), \"N Unique\" = c(3L, 3L, \n    3L), Mean = c(NA, NA, 30), SD = c(NA, NA, 10), Min = c(NA, \n    NA, 20), Max = c(NA, NA, 40)), row.names = c(\"note\", \"pid\", \n\"q3...6\"), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 25, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n## pp1.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Column = c(\"q3\", \"trial\", \"v7\"), Representation = c(\"numeric\", \n\"numeric\", \"numeric\"), Level = c(\"ratio\", \"ratio\", \"ratio\"), \n    Concept = c(\"reaction_time\", \"\", \"condition\"), Role = c(\"measure\", \n    \"measure\", \"measure\"), Unit = c(\"\", \"\", \"\"), Rows = c(6L, \n    6L, 6L), \"% Missing\" = c(0, 0, 0), \"N Unique\" = c(6L, 6L, \n    3L), Mean = c(537, 3.5, 2), SD = c(47.795, 1.871, 0.894), \n    Min = c(490, 1, 1), Max = c(611, 6, 3)), row.names = c(\"q3...3\", \n\"trial...7\", \"v7...10\"), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 25, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n## pp2.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Column = c(\"q3\", \"trial\", \"v7\"), Representation = c(\"numeric\", \n\"numeric\", \"numeric\"), Level = c(\"ratio\", \"ratio\", \"ratio\"), \n    Concept = c(\"reaction_time\", \"\", \"condition\"), Role = c(\"measure\", \n    \"measure\", \"measure\"), Unit = c(\"\", \"\", \"\"), Rows = c(6L, \n    6L, 6L), \"% Missing\" = c(0, 0, 0), \"N Unique\" = c(6L, 6L, \n    3L), Mean = c(538, 3.5, 2), SD = c(47.795, 1.871, 0.894), \n    Min = c(491, 1, 1), Max = c(612, 6, 3)), row.names = c(\"q3...4\", \n\"trial...8\", \"v7...11\"), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 25, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n## pp3.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Column = c(\"q3\", \"trial\", \"v7\"), Representation = c(\"numeric\", \n\"numeric\", \"numeric\"), Level = c(\"ratio\", \"ratio\", \"ratio\"), \n    Concept = c(\"reaction_time\", \"\", \"condition\"), Role = c(\"measure\", \n    \"measure\", \"measure\"), Unit = c(\"\", \"\", \"\"), Rows = c(6L, \n    6L, 6L), \"% Missing\" = c(0, 0, 0), \"N Unique\" = c(6L, 6L, \n    3L), Mean = c(539, 3.5, 2), SD = c(47.795, 1.871, 0.894), \n    Min = c(492, 1, 1), Max = c(613, 6, 3)), row.names = c(\"q3...5\", \n\"trial...9\", \"v7...12\"), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 25, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n:::",
          "LLM model 'mock/dc' reviewed ambiguous cases (0 files, 3 columns) and assigned study groups (1 study group detected).",
          "This module runs automated data-quality checks (outliers, miscoded missing values, empty and constant columns, SPSS filter variables, category casing, problematic column names, mixed text encodings, spreadsheet formatting) on the extracted data files.",
          "We examined 12 columns across 4 data files.",
          "#### Careless Responding",
          "No file could be screened for careless responding.",
          "**What this does not cover.** Only 0 of 4 data files could be screened: the rest had no detectable multi-item scale block, or too few respondents. Even in a screened file, these checks only look at multi-item rating scales — the only place where a repeated or flat answer pattern is interpretable. Single questions, open text, demographics and any item outside a detected scale block are never examined. A respondent can therefore answer most of a survey carelessly and still not be flagged here, and finding nothing is not evidence that a dataset is free of careless responding."
